{{Short description|none}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=April 2017}}{{Use British English|date=April 2017}}
[[File:EarlyCeltic.jpg|thumb|right|An early team photo of [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]], before the adoption of the now-famous hooped jerseys.]]
[[Celtic F.C.|Celtic Football Club]] is a professional [[association football]] club based [[Glasgow]], Scotland. The club was founded in 1887 and began playing league football in 1890 as founder members of the [[Scottish Football League]]. Since their first season Celtic have remained in the top division of the [[Scottish football league system]]: the Scottish Football League (1890–93), [[Scottish Football League|Scottish Football League Division One]] (1893–1975), [[Scottish Football League Premier Division]] (1975–98), [[Scottish Premier League]] (1998–2013) and [[Scottish Premiership]] (2013–present).<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/23435136 |title=SPFL: New Scottish league brands unveiled |date=24 July 2013 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |accessdate=11 August 2016}}</ref> As of [[2022–23 Celtic F.C. season|2022–23]] the club has completed [[List of Celtic F.C. seasons|134 seasons]] of competitive football and have been [[List of Scottish football champions|Scottish football champions]] 54 times.<ref>{{cite web |url=http://spfl.co.uk/clubs/celtic/#honours |title=Celtic Football Club (Honours) |publisher=[[Scottish Professional Football League]] |accessdate=10 August 2016}}</ref>

Celtic played their inaugural league fixture as part of the [[1890–91 Scottish Football League]] on 23 August 1890 against [[Heart of Midlothian F.C.|Heart of Midlothian]]. Since that game they have faced 45 different sides in league football with their most regular opponent having been their [[Old Firm]] rivals [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]], whom they have played on 330 occasions since their first league meeting on 21 March 1891.<ref name="Soccerbase v Rangers">{{cite web |url=http://www.soccerbase.com/teams/head_to_head.sd?team_id=2104&team2_id=512 |title=Head to head – Rangers vs. Celtic |publisher=[[Racing Post|Soccerbase]] |accessdate=10 August 2016}}</ref> They met their most recent different league opponent, [[Ross County F.C.|Ross County]], for the first time in the [[2012–13 Scottish Premier League]] season.<ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/sport/football/teams/celtic/9484993/Ross-County-1-1-Celtic-match-report.html |title=Ross County 1-1 Celtic: match report |first=Roddy |last=Forsyth |date=18 August 2012 |newspaper=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |accessdate=11 August 2016}}</ref> The club has won 180 of the league matches against [[Motherwell F.C.|Motherwell]] which represents the most Celtic have won against any club. They have drawn more matches with Rangers than with any other club with 90 of their meetings finishing without a winner.<ref name="Soccerbase v Rangers"/> Rangers are also the side that has defeated Celtic in more league games than any other club, having won 127 of their encounters.<ref name="Soccerbase v Rangers"/>

==Key==
* The table includes results of matches played by Celtic in the [[Scottish Football League]], [[Scottish Football League First Division|Scottish First Division]], [[Scottish Premier League]] and [[Scottish Premiership]].
* {{legend2|#FFDDFF||border=1px solid #AAAAAA}} {{dagger|alt=Scottish Premiership team}} Teams with this background and symbol in the "Club" column are competing in the [[2023–24 Scottish Premiership]] alongside Celtic.
* {{legend2|#87CEEB||border=1px solid #AAAAAA}} {{double-dagger|alt=defunct}} Clubs with this background and symbol in the "Club" column are defunct
* Pld = matches played; W = matches won; D = matches drawn; L = matches lost; GF = goals for; GA = goals against; Win% = percentage of total matches won
* The columns headed "First" and "Last" contain the first and most recent seasons in which Celtic played league matches against each opponent

